  "title": "SC asks Centre to take measures against misuse of court videos",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court asked the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY) to include penalties for unauthorised circulation of live-streamed court proceedings, while considering safeguards against misuse and commercial exploitation. The court also directed the Centre to incorporate measures for taking action against violations of its interim restrictions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court directed the Centre to incorporate measures for taking action against violations of its interim restrictions on the unauthorised extraction, dissemination and commercial exploitation of live-streamed court proceedings in the proposed policy framework.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The solicitor general sought to include penalties for unauthorised circulation of court hearing videos, considering safeguards against misuse and commercial exploitation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court directed the Centre to consider the suggestions from various high courts and stakeholders for the preparation of comprehensive guidelines.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
